 "summary": "The local-frames presentation of the trivial core and the half-twisted disc pairs are new, and they reuse the existing API: `isRealAlong_iff_coordChange_star`, `smulLeft`, `maslovIndex_eq_of_iso`, `maslovIndex_trivial` and Mathlib's complex log/power lemmas. None of the existing constructors (`constIso`, `isoTrivialOfCoordChangeEqId`, `isoOfContinuousEquiv`) directly replaces `LocalFrames.isoTrivial`, since the first two need constant or identity transitions and the third needs a proof of continuity on the whole total space.",
